## 2. Matched compute: analytic multiplier and the grid snapshot it needs (cheaper cell read at m x U_P)
  (a) between the cells of a step, same arm (larger / smaller):
      F-OQ    1024->  4096:  1.21 -> grid 1.25
      F-OQ    4096-> 16384:  1.70 -> grid 2.0
      T-OQ    1024->  4096:  1.01 -> grid 1.25
      T-OQ    4096-> 16384:  1.04 -> grid 1.25
      H8      1024->  4096:  1.01 -> grid 1.25
      H8      4096-> 16384:  1.03 -> grid 1.25
  (b) dense against the arm at one cell (D-OQ / arm); the arm is the cheaper and is read at m x U_P <= its run length 6 x U_P:
      F-OQ  N=  1024:  1.19 -> grid 1.25
      F-OQ  N=  4096:  1.65 -> grid 2.0
      F-OQ  N= 16384:  2.53 -> grid 3.0
      T-OQ  N=  1024:  1.23 -> grid 1.25
      T-OQ  N=  4096:  2.04 -> grid 2.5
      T-OQ  N= 16384:  5.10 -> grid 6.0
      H8    N=  1024:  1.28 -> grid 1.5
      H8    N=  4096:  2.13 -> grid 2.5
      H8    N= 16384:  5.39 -> grid 6.0
  measured CPU-time multipliers exist only for F-OQ and D-OQ at 16,384 (0.0245 / 0.0158-0.0175 = 1.40-1.55) and F-OQ 16,384/4,096 (1.60-1.65).

